---
import Code from "../../components/Code.astro";
import ReadingTime from "@plugdash/readtime/ReadingTime.astro";
import InstallCommand from "../../components/InstallCommand.astro";
import PluginReference from "../../components/PluginReference.astro";
import { loadDemoEntry } from "../../data/demo-entry";
import { pluginDocToc } from "../../data/doc-toc";
import { getPlugin } from "../../data/plugins";
import Doc from "../../layouts/Doc.astro";

const plugin = getPlugin("readtime")!;
const demo = await loadDemoEntry();
const tocEntries = pluginDocToc.filter((e) => e.id !== "register");
---

<Doc
  tocEntries={tocEntries}
  currentSlug="readtime"
  title="readtime"
  section="@plugdash/readtime"
  description="Reading time and word count for EmDash posts."
>
  <h2 id="what-it-does">What it does</h2>
  <p>
    Counts the words in your post's Portable Text body when the page
    renders and shows the reading time in minutes (238 words per minute,
    minimum 1). CJK text is counted per character. Nothing is stored and
    no JavaScript is sent to the browser. Ships
    <code>ReadingTime.astro</code> with four variants.
  </p>

  <h2 id="install">Install</h2>
  <InstallCommand command={plugin.installCommand} />
  <p>
    There is nothing to register. readtime has no hooks, so you do not add
    it to <code>astro.config.mjs</code>. An older config that still calls
    <code>readtimePlugin()</code> keeps working.
  </p>

  <h2 id="add-the-component">Add the component</h2>
  <p>In your post layout, pass the entry from <code>getEmDashEntry()</code>:</p>
  <Code language="astro" code={`---
import { getEmDashEntry } from "emdash"
import ReadingTime from "@plugdash/readtime/ReadingTime.astro"

const { entry: post } = await getEmDashEntry("posts", Astro.params.slug)
---
<ReadingTime post={post} />`} />
  <p>
    The body field is found on its own: <code>content</code>, then
    <code>body</code>, then the first Portable Text array. Pass
    <code>field="..."</code> if yours is named something else.
  </p>

  <h2 id="live-demo">Live demo</h2>
  {demo ? (
    <>
      <p>All four variants, rendered from a real post on this site:</p>
      <div class="demo-inline">
        <div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:1rem;align-items:center">
          <ReadingTime post={demo} variant="inline" />
          <ReadingTime post={demo} variant="badge" />
          <ReadingTime post={demo} variant="pill" />
          <ReadingTime post={demo} variant="minimal" />
        </div>
      </div>
    </>
  ) : (
    <p>The demo post is not published yet.</p>
  )}

  <PluginReference plugin={plugin} />

  <h2 id="for-agents">For agents</h2>
  <p>
    After installing @plugdash/readtime, import
    <code>ReadingTime.astro</code> in the post layout and render
    <code>&lt;ReadingTime post=&#123;post&#125; /&gt;</code>. Do not
    register a plugin. Open a published post and check the reading time
    shows. If nothing renders, the post has no Portable Text body the
    component can find: pass <code>field</code> with the field name.
    Data stored: none.
  </p>
</Doc>
